pltlocal_aarch64.so -- the GH-1342 fixture for a call through a PLT stub that
the image's own relocation binds to a function it defines
(decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/pltlocal_cli.rs, tests/stages/kuna-pltlocal.xml).

What it is
  A 2,528-byte AArch64 ELF shared object assembled from pltlocal_aarch64.s,
  which is the issue's standalone reproducer verbatim. `timer_wrapper`
  (0x10308) calls `timer_helper@plt` (0x10380) with its own x0, x1, w2 and w3
  untouched and tail-jumps to `send_helper@plt` (0x10390); the
  R_AARCH64_JUMP_SLOT relocations of their GOT slots (0x30468, 0x30470) name
  the defined `timer_helper` (0x10344) and `send_helper` (0x10354).

Why it is vendored
  The host carries no AArch64 assembler or linker, so the object is checked in
  rather than built at test time.

Where it came from
  clang 23.1.4 and LLD 23.1.4 from the mstorsjo/llvm-mingw docker image
  (sha256:dadd757c364edee190c53d8e71a135892a6986182e873205d3611f85e26f290b):

      clang --target=aarch64-linux-gnu -c pltlocal_aarch64.s -o p.o
      ld.lld -shared -o pltlocal_aarch64.so p.o

  sha256 cbd01bf6f90cd6cc36ffb651f6b898acdd6147f998486a24379d4c679a5fcbfb.
